title: FirstLoopBoat
---
<< LightOff Boat >>

<< if DoesHeKnow("SecondLoop") == true >>
	<<jump SecondLoopBoat>>
<<endif>>

<< if DoesHeKnow("BoatguyIntroSeen")>>
	(Enter DR. BOATGUY PHD)
	<<jump tree1>>
<<else>>
	<< Learn BoatguyTarot >>
	<< Learn BoatguyInfoA >> //An.. eccentric ferryman!
	SETTING - The corner by an alleyway across the train station, which leads to a seemingly abandoned pier. The air is damp and thick. The air filled with noise of water lapping at the lakeshore.

	AT RISE - SASHA walks past the alleyway, only to be stopped by a hiss from a shrouded figure hiding in the alleyway.

	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Psst, hey, kid. Over here!
	
	<<if $TechMajor == true>>
		TECH: A wayfarer, or ferryman. You remember when you were growing up this was one of the jobs you desperately wanted to have as your own. 
	<<elseif $PsyMajor == true>>
		PSY: It's just a ferryman. This work once a specialty, a task only delegated to those most well-versed with rivers and in line with religious ideals. Now, it seems to be booming business-- and they have to fight for your attention. 
	<<elseif $ArtMajor == true>>
		ART: A ferryman. You recognize one thing for sure- [i]this[/i] particular ferryman has an eye for the dramatics. 
	<<endif>>


	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Just ten moneys, I’ll give you a ride from all the way point A to B.
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: What are points A and B? That’s up to you- but I’m the cheapest. Don’t listen to the others. Seriously, they’ll chat your ear off. Real annoying if you ask me.


	->"Who are you?"
		SASHA: "Who are you?"
	->"Why are you like this?"
		SASHA: "Why are you like this?
		<<set $sashaDick = true>>


	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Hm? Oh! I’m Dr. Boatguy phD. Quite the celebrity around here if you ask me-- 
	(They spread their arms as far as they can go.)
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: (amused) But you can ask me a lot, really. 

	->"You have a doctorate?"	
		SASHA: "You have a doctorate?"
	->"Boatguy? Is that your real name?"
		SASHA: "Boatguy? Is that your real name?"

	DR. BOATGUY PHD: (smirking) Allegedly.
	(Grin slowly falls as SASHA remains unamused.)
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: [i]Anyway[/i]. So kid, since you’re not begging me to consider you for a ride in my boat, what else can I do ya for? Really, you can ask me a lot. I’m a bit of a….
	(Gestures vaguely)
	(As you open your mouth to answer for them, they cut you off.)
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: [i]Tour guide[/i]! Right. Anyway, what can I do ya for?
	<<jump tree1>>
<<endif>>


===
title: tree1
---

->"What’s the best place to go here?"
	SASHA: "What's the best place to go here?"
	<<jump bestplacetogo>>
->"Okay but- [i]why[/i] are you like this?" <<if $sashaDick is true>>
	SASHA: "Okay but- [i]why[/i] are you like this?"
	<<jump sashawhywouldyousaythat>>
->"I’m looking for my brother, Dmitriy."
	SASHA: "I'm looking for my brother, Dmitriy."
	<<jump wheresdmitriy>>
   
===
title: bestplacetogo
---
DR. BOATGUY PHD: (lets out a low whistle.) Well damn, kid. You’re asking me a lot just by one question. The best, the best? Solster is always the best, know that?
(DR. BOATGUY PHD lets out a long, thoughtful hum, stroking their chin before their finger jots up.)
DR. BOATGUY PHD: So you’d think, right, that the best thing is the parade? Naw, naw, ‘round here, it’s the food! Good stuff, really.
(They point at you, halting all dialogue with a heavy pause.)
DR. BOATGUY PHD: “You look new here, and I don’t mean in the ‘you’re an outsider’ new, but like in the ‘you look like a newborn foal who’s seeing the greenest pasture of its life’ new. Is this your first time in Solster?”
NARRATOR: You remember vaguely meeting Boat before.. They were one of your brother’s friends, you’re sure.
NARRATOR: They don’t seem to share that remembrance, clearly.


//Dialogue Tree 2
-> I’m not new, I grew up here.
    DR. BOATGUY PHD: (baffled) ..Seriously? Then why are you asking me what the best place to go is?
    <<jump tree1>>
-> Well, sort of.
    DR. BOATGUY PHD: Hell yeah! I’ve got an eye for this stuff, really. My mother always told me; Boats- she’d call me that, Boats. It’s hilarious- but she said, Boats! You’re too damn perceptive for your own good. And I’d tell her- yeah well ma! I do like lookin’ at people and figurin’ out what their mind’s all about. Riveting stuff.”

DR. BOATGUY PHD: (clears throat) ..What did you ask again?
(Before you can open your mouth to reply, DR. BOATGUY PHD continues talking.)
DR. BOATGUY PHD: Right! Right. Where you gotta go.. You can try the local café this side of the river! It’s not nearly as good as half of the other ones otherside, but they blocked off the road ‘cos of the parade.
(DR. BOATGUY PHD juts their chin in the direction of a small, dimly lit restaurant on the cornerstone of the street.)
DR. BOATGUY PHD: (Lets out a disdainful sniff) Look, I aint sayin’ it’s bad- it’s edible, really! Just folks think they’re.. Well, we’ve all got our opinions on what’s the best food, eh? Just think the train supply is always a bit too eager to give them first pick. But whatever- I’m just a ferryman, what do I know?
(Pauses for just long enough that you think they're about to stop, but they continue talking right as you open your mouth.)
DR. BOATGUY PHD: And the [i]owner[/i]! Pfah, it's like he's a character in and of itself. Kicked me out of his restaurant once, he did. Because I [i]talked too much[/i] he said.
DR. BOATGUY PHD: We've been mortal enemies ever since.
(They stop talking now. You clear your throat to speak again, expecting another interruption that never comes.)
<<jump tree1>>

===
title: sashawhywouldyousaythat
---
DR. BOATGUY PHD: Uh,
(Dramatically looks around the invisible audience.)
DR. BOATGUY PHD: (unsure) Because it’s funny?
<<jump tree1>>


===
title: wheresdmitriy
---

DR. BOATGUY PHD: Oh! Dmi-
DR. BOATGUY PHD: Dmi-
DR. BOATGUY PHD: Your broth-
DR. BOATGUY PHD: You’re–
DR. BOATGUY PHD: [i]Huh?[/i]
(DR. BOATGUY PHD falls silent for a few moments, before breaking out into a wide grin)

DR. BOATGUY PHD: You’re Dmitriy’s [i]sibling[/i], are you? Oh my goodness! He’ll be so excited to see you’re back!

NARRATOR: Their excitement, while a little overwhelming, is equally as infectious. For a moment you can truly and deeply believe someone’s excited to see you.
(Another silence falls for a few moments)
DR. BOATGUY PHD: (hesitant) Has he.. He’s... Um, I think he should be near the parade, actually! He's on break now, though..
-> "Is something the matter?"
	SASHA: "Is something the matter?"
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: (trying not to smile) The matter? No, no.. not at all…
	NARRATOR: The ferryman is horribly unsubtle, but it's clear that there’s no use trying to pry this information out of them. 
	NARRATOR: You’ll find out sooner or later, whether you want to or not.
	-> Alright then.
	-> Great.
-> Okay.. thanks. 
(DR. BOATGUY PHD nods vehemently, giving a big wave.)
DR. BOATGUY PHD: Say hi for me when you see him!

===
title: SecondLoopBoat
---

DR. BOATGUY PHD: Psst, hey, kid. Over here! Just ten moneys, I’ll give you a ride from all the way point A to B. What are points A and B? That’s up to you- but I’m the cheapest. Don’t listen to the others. Seriously, they’ll chat your ear off. Real annoying if you ask me.

-> "Could you tell me about something?"
	SASHA: "Could you tell me about something?"
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Mhm? What is it?
	<<jump MisinformationBoat>>
-> "I just went back in time, I think. I'm reliving the same day."
	SASHA: "I just went back in time, I think. I'm reliving the same day."
	(Boatguy raises their eyebrows.)
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Ohhh, uh-huh? Dude, I was [i]waiting[/i] for this day to come, seriously!
	NARRATOR: Their eyes start sparkling with a sudden, unadulterated glee.
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: (Quickly) Is it.. can you do that all the time? Like.. Go back in time? See the past? The dinosaurs?
	-> "No.. just back to when I came here."
		Sasha: "No, just when I came here."
		(Boatguy beams.)
	-> "You seem to be enjoying this way too much."
		SASHA: "You seem to be enjoying this way too much."
		NARRATOR: You're upset, naturally. You just watched everybody die and here's Boatguy bouncing up and down like you're a creature of legend. 
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Dude, dude, seriously. You know- I was prepared for this exact moment.
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Next time you come see me, seriously, tell me my secret word. I have a secret word for this! Then- then I'll be like, (pauses to gasp for breath)
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: "Your best friend, I think."
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: The secret word is uh, it's Sisyphus.
	<<if $ArtMajor == true>>
		What a decadently pretentious word for a man like Boatguy. As an Art major, you can truly appreciate that type of dissipation <<if $ArtMajor == true>>
	<<endif>>
	<<if $TechMajor == true>>
		Sisyphus? [i]Seriously?[/i]
	<<endif>>
	NARRATOR: Regardless, it would be nice to have someone on your side without having to have this entire conversation again. An oddly helpful thing from the resident nutcase.
	-> "Noted."
		Sasha: "Noted."
	-> "..Sure."
		Sasha: "..Sure."
	(DR. BOATGUY PHD nods)
	<<set $DudeTheyJustSaidThat = true>>
	<< Learn BoatguyInfoD >> //Their secret word is "sisyphus"
-> "That’s alright."
-> "Hey, Boatguy.. Sisyphus." <<if DoesHeKnow("BoatguyInfoD")>>
	<<jump PRANKED>>

===

title: MisinformationBoat
---

-> "What's with (blank)"
	Sasha: "What's with (blank)"
-> "What do you think of (blank)"
	Sasha: "What do you think of (blank)"
-> "Who's (blank)"
	Sasha: "Who's (blank)"
-> "Nevermind"
	Sasha: "Nevermind."
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: "Oh.. okay :("
	<<stop>>

-> "Can I ask you another question?"
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Ahuh?
	<<jump MisinformationBoat>>
-> "Okay, thanks."
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Anytime, kid! (muttering) Seriously, I have nothing better I should be be doing.
<<stop>>
===
title: PRANKED
---
<<if $DudeTheyJustSaidThat == true>>
	(DR. BOATGUY PHD stares at you blankly.)
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Yeah?
	-> "The secret time travel word?"
		Sasha: "The secret time travel word?"
	-> "That's what you told me I should say if I was in a timeloop."
		Sasha: "That's what you told me I should say if I was in a timeloop."
		(They nod, confused.)
			-> "Don't you believe me?"
				Sasha: "Don't you believe me?"
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: Dude.. I JUST told you that.
	ART: Doesn't anyone appreciate trying all the choices in dialogue despite nonsensicality anymore?
	TECH: You're a moron, Sasha.
	PSY: You were just curious as to what they'd say.. now you feel like an idiot.
	<<stop>>
<<else>>
	<<Learn BoatguyInfoB>> //Easily spreads misinformation.
	(DR. BOATGUY PHD stares at you blankly.)
	DR. BOATGUY PHD: "Huh?"
	-> "The secret time travel word?"
		SASHA: "The secret time travel word?"
		DR. BOATGUY PHD: [i]What[/i] are you talking about?
	-> "That's what you told me I should say if I was in a timeloop.
		SASHA: "That's what you told me I should say if I was in a timeloop.
		DR. BOATGUY PHD: What now? No I didn't. (pause) You're stuck in a timeloop?"
	-> "You [i]definitely[/i] told me that."
		SASHA: "You [i]definitely[/i] told me that."
		Dr. Boatguy: Nuh-Uh. What even [i]is[/i] a Sisyphus? I've never heard of that in my life.
		(They cross their arms.)
		DR. BOATGUY PHD: (pouting) Are you making fun of me? What the heck, dude?
		NARRATOR: You suppose that perhaps Boatguy from the last loop had not properly communicated their knowledge.
		ART: Or perhaps you've been.. [i]pranked.[/i]<<if $ArtMajor == true>>
	-> "Oh god damn it, Boatguy.."
<<endif>>

===